# The MENDED tech tree and the economy that places it (docs/VISION.md §6.1),
# through the real keys: a bench turns a landscape's material into a modifier, the
# modifier goes into a socket, the land it was made for stops biting, a machine
# gives up the part it was carrying, and a second modifier changes what the body
# can DO rather than what it resists.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/gear-economy.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --build=bench --held=mono_blade \
#     --give=wick:60,scrap:2,copper:2,bog_iron:1,scarf_mask:1,mod_phase:1
#
# What is in the creel at boot and why. Plate and copper are ordinary stock off
# any tip. The BOG IRON is the moss's own material, and refining it is four peats
# and two hours at a fire, which is a night of world time no tour should spend;
# its gate — peat only comes out of a bank, and banks only stand in the moss — is
# walked in tests/gear_economy/test_obtainable.gd. Everything the modifiers
# themselves do is earned here, in front of the camera.
#
# MEASURED, seed 1. The first CUTTER put down gives up its filament edge
# (GearEconomy.kills_for(&"mono_edge", 1) == 1), so one body is enough, and the
# bonelands is where cutters work.
#
# The THIN BLADE in hand is the other half of that measurement, and two earlier
# versions of this tour are the reason it is there. A clerk has 6 life and looked
# like the easy kill, but a clerk darts — it comes in close, files you and goes,
# and it is faster than a person — so 24 chases with a knife and then 24 with a
# beam both ended with an empty frame and no body in it. A worker on its round
# does not run: it walks, and it can be walked down. A cutter has 70 life, which
# is seven connects at 11 damage, and that is a tour-length fight. The charges are
# sixty because a thin blade spends one a swing and a chase misses: the run before
# this one ended with the cutter alive and the counter on zero.
coast calm
hour 11

# --- 1. A bench turns a landscape's material into a modifier -------------------
await station:bench 8
shot 01-a-bench-on-the-strand with station:bench,land:coast
tap craft
await app:crafting 8
choose mod_cooling
tap use
await made 20
shot 02-a-cooling-loop-off-the-making-page with app:crafting,station:bench
tap craft
await app:none 6

# --- 2. The burning, on a body with nothing between it and the heat ------------
place burning
wait 1.8
await heat 15
await pressure_bites 20
shot 03-the-burning-bites with land:burning,pressure_bites,heat

# --- 3. The loop bound to the blade, on the slate, with the real keys ----------
# The hand's row is the only slot open here, which is the point: no vest, no body
# piece, nothing else keeping the heat off, and the blade itself resists nothing.
# What happens next is the modifier's doing and nothing else's.
tap pause
choose loadout
tap use
await app:loadout 10
shot 04-the-gear-page-before with app:loadout
choose tool
tap use
wait 0.4
await modifier 6
shot 05-the-loop-bound-to-the-blade with app:loadout,modifier
tap pause
tap pause
wait 2.2
await answered:heat 25
shot 06-the-burning-answered with land:burning,answered:heat

# --- 4. The part comes out of the body that was carrying it -------------------
# Round it to its WORKING PART and swing, over and over, the way a player does. A
# cutter carries its part at its back, so met face on it is all plate: a run of
# this tour that used `walkto mob` put twenty-four swings into the front of one
# and rang every single one of them off. The await has to be INSIDE the loop, too:
# nothing else in there can fail, and a `try` whose lines all succeed runs once.
place bonelands
wait 1.5
spawn cutter
shot 07-a-cutter-on-its-round with mob:cutter,land:bonelands
try 26
  walkto part 4
  tap swing
  await killed 1.2
end
# No second `await killed` here: an await CONSUMES the event it waited for
# (98_tour `_seen.erase`), so asking twice fails the second time even though the
# body is lying right there. What is asked instead is a state — the filament edge
# is in the creel — which is the thing this section is actually about.
await elite:mono_edge 5
shot 08-what-it-was-carrying with spoils,land:bonelands

# --- 5. A modifier that changes what the body can DO --------------------------
# A phase coil under a scarf-mask reads the working part through the plate over
# it: the same socket, a power instead of a resistance.
tap pause
choose loadout
tap use
await app:loadout 10
choose head
tap use
wait 0.4
tap use
wait 0.4
await modifier:mod_phase 8
shot 09-a-phase-coil-in-a-head-socket with app:loadout,modifier:mod_phase
tap pause
tap pause
wait 1.0
# Something ALIVE to read: a scan brackets living machines, and the first version
# of this fired it over the cutter it had just killed, so the frame was called a
# reading and held nothing being read.
spawn watcher
wait 0.9
tap ability_scan
await ability:scan 8
wait 0.4
shot 10-a-watcher-read-through-a-socketed-coil with mob:watcher,land:bonelands
